WEBVTT

00:01:32.380 --> 00:01:39.530
The period when the Touda eggs hatch is the busiest time of the year for beastinarians.

00:01:39.990 --> 00:01:44.840
Making a wild egg hatch while under human care is a very difficult task.

00:01:45.380 --> 00:01:48.320
Mom, that was the third time today.

00:01:48.520 --> 00:01:52.900
That's right.  You have to roll them like this every day.

00:01:53.210 --> 00:01:58.800
And we have to control the temperature and moisture, too, right Mom?

00:01:59.380 --> 00:02:00.540
That's right.

00:02:01.270 --> 00:02:03.740
A baby Touda, eh?

00:02:03.740 --> 00:02:05.520
I want to see them hatch soon.

00:02:06.420 --> 00:02:08.530
Okay, that'll do.

00:02:08.530 --> 00:02:10.160
Was it the same for me?

00:02:10.160 --> 00:02:11.220
What?

00:02:11.220 --> 00:02:16.680
Was I kept warm and rolled around in your belly to get big?

00:02:17.690 --> 00:02:18.680
That's right.

00:02:19.640 --> 00:02:24.130
You used to kick my stomach a lot.

00:02:24.130 --> 00:02:25.750
What?

00:02:25.750 --> 00:02:28.710
I had bad sleeping habits even back then?

00:03:58.340 --> 00:03:59.720
Mom?

00:04:02.270 --> 00:04:04.130
You were still awake?

00:04:04.130 --> 00:04:06.180
It's thundering.

00:04:07.330 --> 00:04:11.710
It's fine.  The thunder cloud is on the other side of the mountain.

00:04:13.170 --> 00:04:15.990
Don't worry and go to bed.

00:04:25.050 --> 00:04:26.240
Mom.

00:04:26.550 --> 00:04:29.190
The rain was cold, wasn't it?

00:04:29.770 --> 00:04:31.960
I can smell the rain and the Touda.

00:04:33.540 --> 00:04:34.960
Hey, Mom.

00:04:35.460 --> 00:04:36.850
What is it?

00:04:36.850 --> 00:04:41.760
Can I follow you on the next night patrol for the Touda?

00:04:42.160 --> 00:04:43.280
Let's see...

00:04:46.810 --> 00:04:47.900
Sure.

00:04:49.410 --> 00:04:53.460
It's a...  promise...  okay?

00:05:06.640 --> 00:05:11.740
A screeching sound echoed through the village as if it were trying to wake everyone.

00:05:12.400 --> 00:05:17.590
It sounded as if it was trying to warn of something terrible happening.

00:05:19.780 --> 00:05:25.680
Soyon's Warmth

00:05:31.770 --> 00:05:33.010
Mom?

00:05:33.010 --> 00:05:34.710
You stay here.

00:05:43.980 --> 00:05:47.370
What is this sound?

00:06:08.770 --> 00:06:11.080
It's definitely a Touda funeral cry.

00:06:11.390 --> 00:06:12.140
Let's hurry.

00:06:12.910 --> 00:06:15.100
"Touda funeral cry?"

00:06:47.470 --> 00:06:48.910
What is this smell?

00:07:03.300 --> 00:07:04.610
What is this?

00:07:10.250 --> 00:07:11.350
Mom...

00:07:15.230 --> 00:07:16.500
Is it dead?

00:07:26.530 --> 00:07:28.510
Every one in this pond?

00:07:30.670 --> 00:07:31.700
Chief!

00:07:32.300 --> 00:07:35.270
A Kiba's dead in the adjacent pond, too!

00:07:36.620 --> 00:07:38.140
How about the other Touda?

00:07:38.140 --> 00:07:40.010
The others are all fine.

00:07:40.010 --> 00:07:45.170
They ceased the funeral cry, but they're all swimming around in panic.

00:07:45.710 --> 00:07:51.010
They'll scar their hides by scratching against the wall if they swim in a panic.

00:07:51.010 --> 00:07:54.160
Everyone!  Head to the pond you're in charge of!

00:07:54.160 --> 00:07:55.030
Yes!

00:07:55.030 --> 00:07:55.920
Let's go.

00:07:55.920 --> 00:07:58.960
We can't lose any more!

00:08:02.280 --> 00:08:03.720
What's the cause?

00:08:03.720 --> 00:08:05.390
I can't identify it yet.

00:08:05.390 --> 00:08:08.470
Did it suffocate from the washu?

00:08:08.470 --> 00:08:09.050
No.

00:08:09.500 --> 00:08:11.020
The gills are clear.

00:08:11.020 --> 00:08:14.080
The washu must have arrived after it died.

00:08:14.080 --> 00:08:17.770
You were providing benetrophic water regularly, right?

00:08:18.290 --> 00:08:21.170
You didn't see anything strange when made your rounds?

00:08:23.660 --> 00:08:27.570
It's a felony to let all the Kiba die!

00:08:35.190 --> 00:08:36.490
I'm prepared to accept the punishment.

00:08:38.280 --> 00:08:39.960
"Prepared," you say?

00:08:42.530 --> 00:08:45.420
Then I guess I have to be as well.

00:08:47.490 --> 00:08:49.250
M-Mom?

00:08:53.060 --> 00:08:54.460
Mom?

00:08:54.460 --> 00:08:55.850
It's fine.

00:08:55.850 --> 00:08:58.060
But he said it's a felony!

00:08:58.330 --> 00:08:59.600
Don't worry.

00:09:00.050 --> 00:09:06.430
There was a case where all the Kiba died when your great-grandfather was in charge.

00:09:07.300 --> 00:09:10.440
Kiba are more susceptible to disease than other Touda.

00:09:10.440 --> 00:09:13.700
That's something everyone knows.

00:09:36.680 --> 00:09:38.470
Thank you, Erin.

00:09:38.470 --> 00:09:39.330
Mom...

00:09:41.620 --> 00:09:44.140
Do Touda smell different when they die?

00:09:45.520 --> 00:09:49.770
Or did the smell change because they're sick?

00:09:51.530 --> 00:09:54.160
Erin, what made you come up with that?

00:09:54.680 --> 00:09:55.830
Well...

00:09:57.160 --> 00:10:00.170
It smells differently than usual.

00:10:00.170 --> 00:10:04.940
That's why I thought that maybe those flies were attracted to it.

00:10:09.140 --> 00:10:10.110
Anything else?

00:10:12.550 --> 00:10:18.100
I've seen washu in the water often, but I've never seen flies like this here before.

00:10:18.510 --> 00:10:23.450
Flowers carry different scents depending on the kind, and that's why different bugs are attracted to them, right?

00:10:23.450 --> 00:10:28.110
Isn't it because the Touda's scent changed that these flies were attracted here?

00:10:29.410 --> 00:10:30.390
Erin...

00:10:32.180 --> 00:10:33.500
You're...

00:10:34.990 --> 00:10:39.300
Erin, don't tell anyone what you just said.

00:10:39.300 --> 00:10:40.550
Why not?

00:10:40.550 --> 00:10:41.490
No matter what.

00:10:43.680 --> 00:10:47.300
Being sharp can bring disaster at times.

00:10:49.430 --> 00:10:52.370
You'll understand one day.

00:10:55.000 --> 00:10:55.800
Okay.

00:10:56.060 --> 00:10:57.560
I won't tell anyone.

00:11:31.670 --> 00:11:34.740
Great!  Lulu's safe!

00:11:34.740 --> 00:11:38.200
Erin, you head on back.

00:11:40.850 --> 00:11:43.390
I still have things to do.

00:11:43.390 --> 00:11:47.340
Change out of your clothes and wait at Saju's place.

00:11:49.440 --> 00:11:51.920
Good thing Lulu was safe!

00:11:54.360 --> 00:11:55.900
Hey Erin, you're not going to eat any more?

00:11:56.270 --> 00:11:57.920
Don't mind if I take it, do you?

00:11:57.920 --> 00:11:59.720
I bet you'll live a good long life.

00:11:59.720 --> 00:12:02.050
Hey!  Both of you, eat and behave!

00:12:03.030 --> 00:12:05.100
<i>It's a felony...</i>

00:12:07.250 --> 00:12:08.730
Felony...

00:12:09.500 --> 00:12:12.670
Oba-san, what's going to happen to Mom?

00:12:13.380 --> 00:12:15.210
Is she going to get a severe punishment?

00:12:16.330 --> 00:12:19.940
Relax.  Don't worry and eat your meal.

00:12:19.940 --> 00:12:24.690
She's right.  Here.  This pickle is well brined.

00:12:24.690 --> 00:12:25.950
Let me try one.

00:12:27.060 --> 00:12:28.280
Wow, it's sour!

00:12:28.280 --> 00:12:30.290
Isn't it too brined?

00:12:30.290 --> 00:12:32.250
You, keep your mouth shut.

00:12:32.250 --> 00:12:33.140
What are you doing?!

00:12:33.140 --> 00:12:33.450
"What am I...?"
What are you doing?!

00:12:33.450 --> 00:12:34.520
You'll make me stupid!
"What am I...?"

00:12:34.520 --> 00:12:34.760
You'll make me stupid!

00:12:34.760 --> 00:12:35.490
Ugh!
You'll make me stupid!

00:12:35.490 --> 00:12:35.870
Ugh!

00:12:47.800 --> 00:12:49.290
Are you done, Soyon?

00:12:50.810 --> 00:12:54.790
Make them easy to check for when the inspector comes.

00:12:55.460 --> 00:12:58.280
I bet the inspection will be really thorough.

00:12:58.670 --> 00:13:00.500
For both you and the Chief.

00:13:03.170 --> 00:13:06.240
W-When you're finished, come to the assembly hall.

00:13:20.790 --> 00:13:22.570
Erin-chan, Erin-chan.

00:13:22.570 --> 00:13:26.440
This girl wants to be your little sister.

00:13:26.440 --> 00:13:29.370
See?  This one's my little sister.

00:13:29.740 --> 00:13:30.500
Here.

00:13:31.190 --> 00:13:32.140
Hey!

00:13:32.140 --> 00:13:34.020
Fight, Erin doll!

00:13:34.020 --> 00:13:35.840
Beat Saju doll!

00:13:35.840 --> 00:13:36.540
There, take that.

00:13:36.540 --> 00:13:37.320
Hey, give it back!

00:13:37.320 --> 00:13:39.500
Eek, it's Sajugon.
Hey, give it back!

00:13:39.500 --> 00:13:42.760
The inspector will be here by dawn tomorrow.

00:13:42.760 --> 00:13:46.160
What will we do when we've yet to find the reason behind the Kiba's deaths?

00:13:46.410 --> 00:13:50.700
More importantly, Chief.  Who's going to take the punishment for letting the Kiba die?

00:13:52.340 --> 00:13:56.020
Who took the blame last time?

00:13:58.730 --> 00:14:01.270
Was it your father, the previous Chief?

00:14:01.890 --> 00:14:02.990
No.

00:14:02.990 --> 00:14:07.370
The one who took the blame was the one taking care of the Kiba.

00:14:11.560 --> 00:14:12.850
But...

00:14:12.850 --> 00:14:14.700
Soyon has done nothing wrong.

00:14:16.790 --> 00:14:21.510
Then you're saying it's better for the entire village to be blamed for the event and be ostracized?

00:14:24.530 --> 00:14:29.720
Chief, the one taking care of the Kiba who died is your son's wife.

00:14:32.710 --> 00:14:35.480
I'm sure you'll be questioned heavily, too.

00:14:35.480 --> 00:14:36.920
Soyon's of the Mist People, as well.

00:14:37.340 --> 00:14:42.820
They'll ask you why you let an Arryo take care of the Kiba.

00:14:52.840 --> 00:14:53.930
Are you all right?

00:14:53.930 --> 00:14:55.910
It's dangerous, Erin-chan.

00:15:00.990 --> 00:15:02.210
Are you all right, everyone?

00:15:02.650 --> 00:15:04.340
Yeah, we're fine.

00:15:06.850 --> 00:15:11.850
Erin, you don't look so well.  Is somewhere hurting?

00:15:12.970 --> 00:15:16.580
<i>The one who took the blame was the one taking care of the Kiba.</i>

00:15:18.330 --> 00:15:21.240
Rather than me, it's you...

00:15:21.990 --> 00:15:23.780
You're worried because of the meeting?

00:15:24.080 --> 00:15:27.800
It's fine.  You don't have to worry any about it.

00:15:27.800 --> 00:15:29.300
But!

00:15:36.500 --> 00:15:38.060
Mom!

00:15:38.570 --> 00:15:41.020
I won't need it anymore.

00:15:45.620 --> 00:15:48.770
I know you wanted to take care of the Touda,

00:15:49.420 --> 00:15:55.560
but now that I don't have to carry the whistle, I'm relieved.

00:15:56.830 --> 00:15:58.110
Why?

00:15:58.420 --> 00:16:01.290
Did you not like taking care of the Touda?

00:16:02.070 --> 00:16:03.230
It's not that.

00:16:05.210 --> 00:16:08.630
I didn't like using the whistle.

00:16:10.350 --> 00:16:16.810
I really didn't like seeing the Touda petrify the moment I blew the whistle.

00:16:17.640 --> 00:16:21.770
Beasts that are tamed by humans are miserable.

00:16:22.500 --> 00:16:27.900
It was painful to see them getting weaker and weaker.

00:16:28.790 --> 00:16:32.090
Touda become weaker when they're tamed by humans?

00:16:32.090 --> 00:16:35.290
Don't they become stronger with the benetrophic water we give them?

00:16:36.010 --> 00:16:42.940
Yes, their scales and bones become sturdier, but there are things that become weaker.

00:16:44.780 --> 00:16:45.920
What does?

00:16:48.910 --> 00:16:53.120
I'm sure you will find the answer yourself.

00:16:53.540 --> 00:16:58.760
It's something a wild Touda can do, but those living in the ponds can't.

00:17:02.580 --> 00:17:06.640
But, even if you find the answer, don't tell it to anyone.

00:17:07.040 --> 00:17:10.240
It's something other Touda breeders do not know.

00:17:14.240 --> 00:17:17.200
All right, let's go get our bath.

00:17:24.080 --> 00:17:26.480
Soyon, it must have been a horrible day for you.

00:17:26.480 --> 00:17:29.920
We know better than anyone that you work very hard.

00:17:30.400 --> 00:17:33.290
You must be tired.  Have a good soak.

00:17:42.650 --> 00:17:44.720
<i>Soyon's of the Mist People, as well.</i>

00:17:44.720 --> 00:17:46.720
<i>They'll ask you why you let an Arryo...</i>

00:17:49.470 --> 00:17:53.960
Do we always get the last bath because you're an Arryo?

00:17:57.040 --> 00:17:58.400
Is it?

00:17:59.320 --> 00:18:02.310
"Arryo" isn't the actual name.

00:18:03.410 --> 00:18:04.990
"Ar" means "mist."

00:18:04.990 --> 00:18:06.240
"Ryo" means "people."

00:18:06.580 --> 00:18:12.380
The word "Mist People" matched our image, so that's probably why the word spread.

00:18:12.380 --> 00:18:15.160
The real name is Aowrow.

00:18:15.160 --> 00:18:16.850
"Aowrow?"

00:18:16.850 --> 00:18:18.370
"Aow" means "precedent."

00:18:18.370 --> 00:18:20.420
"Row" means "keeper."

00:18:20.420 --> 00:18:21.680
"Precedent?"

00:18:23.930 --> 00:18:29.840
It's a mistake made in the past that we use as an example so it won't be repeated.

00:18:30.180 --> 00:18:37.870
In the Aowrow clan, you protect that example more dearly than your life or the lives of your family.

00:18:38.070 --> 00:18:39.610
What was the mistake?

00:18:40.220 --> 00:18:44.800
A mistake that would cause all humans and beasts to die.

00:18:49.420 --> 00:18:51.900
I'll tell you a story of long, long ago.

00:18:52.170 --> 00:18:57.970
My ancestors swore to pass on the mistake so that we would never face the verge of extinction,

00:18:57.970 --> 00:19:05.560
and so that we could live without serving the Queen, nor the Grand Duke.

00:19:06.830 --> 00:19:12.370
But I met your father and decided to live in this village.

00:19:12.370 --> 00:19:18.290
From that moment on, I ceased to be a Keeper of Precedent, an Aowrow.

00:19:19.970 --> 00:19:23.280
But that's not what everyone thinks, right?

00:19:32.110 --> 00:19:33.400
I'll give that to you.

00:19:33.780 --> 00:19:34.750
But...

00:19:34.750 --> 00:19:37.630
I got it from my mother.

00:19:38.560 --> 00:19:41.600
Can I really have such an important thing?

00:19:42.670 --> 00:19:46.310
I was planning on giving it to you when you grew up.

00:19:54.060 --> 00:20:00.090
I'm sure your mother gave it to you so your hearts would always be connected even when you two were far away.

00:20:06.600 --> 00:20:09.260
Looks like it's still a little too big for you.

00:20:09.260 --> 00:20:12.250
Later, I'll make it so you can wear it like a necklace.

00:20:12.250 --> 00:20:12.980
Okay.

00:20:15.000 --> 00:20:17.550
How does shishi meat sound for supper?

00:20:17.550 --> 00:20:18.790
What?!  Really?!

00:20:18.790 --> 00:20:19.380
Yeah.

00:20:19.590 --> 00:20:22.420
It's not a festival or any celebration.

00:20:22.420 --> 00:20:27.890
Let's eat our stomachs full of meat tonight so we can work hard tomorrow, too.

00:20:28.330 --> 00:20:29.170
Yup!

00:20:32.410 --> 00:20:33.750
It's the smell of miso.

00:20:36.530 --> 00:20:39.790
I've let it sit a long time, so it'll taste good.

00:20:42.260 --> 00:20:45.260
You put the shishi meat on top of the laco leaf.

00:20:45.670 --> 00:20:48.540
On top of that, you put the lacos' fruit.

00:22:22.410 --> 00:22:23.800
It's so warm.

00:22:28.250 --> 00:22:29.550
Mom.

00:22:30.290 --> 00:22:32.230
What do I smell like?

00:22:33.190 --> 00:22:34.960
Let's see...

00:22:34.960 --> 00:22:36.690
Smells like the sun.

00:22:38.150 --> 00:22:43.610
You're father was like the sun, too, when he smiled.

00:22:45.520 --> 00:22:48.620
Smells...  like the sun...

00:22:49.800 --> 00:22:50.890
Good night.

00:22:52.910 --> 00:22:56.370
I want to keep... talking a little more...

00:22:57.290 --> 00:23:00.290
with...  you...

00:23:11.090 --> 00:23:12.140
It's here.

00:23:14.160 --> 00:23:17.070
You're the one who was taking care of the Kiba that died?

00:23:17.070 --> 00:23:17.900
Yes.

00:23:17.900 --> 00:23:19.520
Come.  We need to question you.

00:23:24.970 --> 00:23:26.220
Mom?!

00:23:26.990 --> 00:23:28.320
Mom!

00:23:35.640 --> 00:23:36.830
Erin...

00:23:36.830 --> 00:23:38.130
Mom!

00:23:38.130 --> 00:23:39.290
You can't go.

00:23:41.920 --> 00:23:43.880
No!  Mom!

00:23:43.880 --> 00:23:45.340
Mom!

00:23:45.340 --> 00:23:48.040
MOM!

00:24:02.010 --> 00:24:05.610
A herd of Touda causes ripples in the silent water.

00:24:05.610 --> 00:24:08.810
I'm in the cold, dark water.

00:24:08.810 --> 00:24:11.140
I won't ever be able to meet Erin again.

00:24:11.620 --> 00:24:15.700
But she comes, attempting to save me.

00:24:16.120 --> 00:24:18.110
Erin, live.

00:24:18.620 --> 00:24:20.640
Live, and find your happiness.

00:24:21.500 --> 00:24:24.960
Kemono no Souja Erin.  Mother's Whistle.

00:24:24.960 --> 00:24:29.980
Mother's Whistle
